|name1 = Frozen Rose Cat
|name2 = Arctic Bloom Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Arctic Bloom Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Frozen Rose Cat is ultimately underwhelming. Like most anti-Zombie Ubers, they have excellent compatibility against zombie midrangers and melee threats, but Frozen Rose's lack of base health, defensive abilities and vulnerability to zombie abilities can easily dismiss their only relevant strengths.

They are a variant of Ice Cat, who's a solid Backlining Crowd-Controlling unit with a similar ability, and they have a very promising niche that freezes Zombies with a good chance of activation and decent uptime. Despite this, their range doesn't save them from being annihilated by their target trait.

First of all, even though they have decent range on paper, considering that almost all Zombie enemies can burrow, their range can be bypassed easily by many Zombies that would end up either inside or past their hitbox, resulting in either their death, or them being clipped through. You may be able to bypass this with meatshielding, which triggers the burrow, but it's almost impossible to properly do with Zombies that burrow more than once. Their attack animation is painfully long, and mostly the enemies would burrow past or get past your meatshields by then, making their attack miss Zombies anyway.

Their slow immune is interesting, which can really help against the likes of Croakley, but their three matchups against [[Daboo of the Dead|Daboo]], [[Lophiiformes Angaburu|Angaburu]] and [[Zomboe]] are not great. Daboo is Immune to Freeze (though they could still be of some use against Zombie peons that support Daboo in [[Parade of the Dead (Deadly)|Parade of the Dead]]/[[Prisoner's Progress (Merciless)|Prisoner's Progress]]) and hits with 800 range Omni Strikes that spell out doom for them. Zomboe burrows, and Angaburu can rip through them with its frequently spawning Mini-Surges. Thus, they cannot counter many Zombies on late game stages, as they are decimated very easily by Zombies, and they only have a subpar and situational usage as a Crowd-Controlling Semi-Nuker for Zombie Outbreak stages from Empire of Cats and early Into the Future.

